//! Phase 7 cross-validation gate: iris (real sklearn data), a
//! digits-scale LCG dataset, and a 5000-sample LCG dataset (exercising the
//! iterative LOBPCG spectral path), fit against the Python baseline
//! references (generated by `/tmp/opencode/cv/gen_phase7_refs.py` and
//! `/tmp/opencode/cv/gen_phase7_large_ref.py` from the umap repo).
//!
//! Parity is statistical (see `tests/e2e_fit.rs`): trustworthiness within
//! ±0.02 of Python (iris: 0.96098, lcg1797: 0.93662, lcg5000: 0.92511).
//! Note Python's own
//! run-to-run variance at the 1797-sample scale is ~1e-3 (numba's
//! parallel `smooth_knn_dist` reductions are unsynchronized even with
//! `random_state` set); the tolerance covers it.
#![allow(clippy::unreadable_literal, clippy::excessive_precision)]

